# Focal antipedal invariant k603

The complete telescoping proof and original receipt are unchanged. The pending-review header predates the included independent PASS audit. For nondegenerate Poncelet orbits between nested confocal ellipses, the sums of ordinary distances from each focus to its antipedal vertices are equal for every N. A per-edge difference is a fixed coefficient times vertical displacement. No hyperbolic-caustic extension or individual-sum constancy is claimed.

Run `python verify.py` here and `python independent_checks.py` inside independent_review. The reviewer independently derived the identity using unit-normal chord coordinates and verified the primary source, signs and orientation. Intended claimed_solved 2/5; novelty unestablished, no human peer-review claim. Source PDFs are excluded.
